					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-622433#post-2088876</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-622433/the-bloody-autumn#post-2088876</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 14 Aug 2014 18:23:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DJ Drowsy Bear</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1950419</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like most of the ideas in this canon, but I don't really think having a scarecrow with a pipe is the right way to go. These SCPs are supposed to be the four horsemen of the apocalypse. Not the four sociopath murderers with anomalous traits. Granted, there are a lot of other armageddon-like things happening in this story, but out of everything, I'd be more worried of the frost giants in Scandinavia, the Leviathan near Africa, or the dozens of other catastrophic events going on than I would be of a group of walking ghosts. Don't get me wrong, it'd be terrifying, but on a world-wide scale? It's not nearly as problematic.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
